  "semantics": {
    "coarse_sample": "launch_flags bit 4 selects a streaming variant's coarse-sample build (manifest entries with coarse_sample true, symbol suffix _cs): its sampled first pass reads one 64-byte block per 512 bytes of the row (1/8) instead of one per 256 (1/4), with the lower-bucket margin, the sampled-mass cap and the filter-arm density switch scaled to the rate; the exact passes and the fallbacks are unchanged, so every output is bit-identical to the default build; the host sets it for launches whose largest top-k is at most fused_tail_kcap (rows at the gather capacity, k ~ 1000, lose with the coarser estimate)",
    "determinism": "strict: no atomics decide any output; slab (vals, idx) is rewritten in sorted order and renorm_out is emitted in that order, bitwise identical across launches, CUDA-graph replay and every kernel variant",
    "early_trigger": "launch_flags bit 1 makes stage 1 issue griddepcontrol.launch_dependents early (register-resident variants: once the row is in registers; streaming variants: see stream_prepass) so a PDL-chained stage-2/3 launch starts on the SMs this grid leaves free; the host sets it only when batch <= sm_count - (batch * cluster mod sm_count, or sm_count) so the dependent CTAs are not packed onto a few SMs; otherwise the trigger is left to CTA exit",
    "fused_tail": "stage 1 takes the stage-2/3 parameters and a host launch_flags word (bit 0 = fuse the tail, bit 1 = early PDL trigger, bit 2 = stream pre-pass trigger point); on a variant whose entry has fused_tail true, bit 0 set and max top-k <= fused_tail_kcap runs every row's stage 2/3 inside the stage-1 kernel (warp 0 of rank 0 after one cluster barrier) with the same outputs, and the stage-2/3 kernel is not launched; variants with fused_tail false (the ept = 48 resident, a large-k pick) are built without the tail and reject bit 0",
    "nan_inf": "NaN, negative and -0.0 probabilities are sanitized to +0 and never sampled; a row containing +inf keeps exactly its +inf entries, samples uniformly among them and renormalizes to 1/m; a zero-mass row returns its smallest slab index with an all-zero renorm",
    "rng": "one curand_uniform per row from curand_init(seed, row, offset) (Philox4x32-10); a shared torch.Generator is advanced by 32 * batch like the FlashInfer top-p routes",
    "stream_prepass": "launch_flags bit 2 selects the streaming variants' early-trigger site: with bits 1 and 2 they trigger before the first (sampled) pass, with bit 1 alone after the filter pass (once the whole row has been read); the host sets bit 2 on compute capability >= 10 (Blackwell, Rubin) and leaves it clear on Hopper; residents ignore it",
    "top_k": "first k entries of lexsort(-prob, index): k largest sanitized probabilities, ties toward the lower vocabulary index; k clamped to [1, min(vocab, slab_entries)]",
    "top_p": "shortest sorted prefix whose exclusive exact fixed-point mass is below p * mass(top-k), renormalized in float64; p clamped to (0, 1] (p <= 0 -> argmax, NaN -> 1)"
  },
